  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.3. Increased institutional capacity and resilience of labour administrations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development of a Paperless Labour Inspection System in Fiji in partnership with the Ministry of Employment Productivity and Industrial Relations has enhanced the effectiveness of enforcement actions by identifying high-risk sectors and prioritizing inspections based on data analysis. 

The newly developed system facilitates better coordination and communication among different departments and agencies involved in labour regulation and enforcement which increases transparency and accountability in labour inspection processes by providing a centralized and accessible platform for recording and tracking inspection results.

It streamlines administrative processes and reduces paperwork through digital record-keeping and automated reporting and further it provides timely and accurate information and further supports the development of evidence-based policies and regulations by providing comprehensive and up-to-date data on labour conditions and compliance levels which fosters a culture of compliance. The ILO supported the development of the paperless system with the help of an IT company until October 2023 to develop the system in line with standard ILS operating procedures set out by the Fiji government. The ILO in collaboration with the MEPIR conducted an initial assessment of its inspection processes, identifying and mapping the procedural workflow and standard operating procedures of the inspectorate after which the system was designed.</narrative>
   </description>
